  "problem": "A bag of cement of mass $30\\,\\text{kg}$ falls vertically downward. Let $v$ be its velocity, with downward taken as the positive direction.\nThe air resistance on the bag is proportional to the square of its velocity and acts in the opposite direction to the direction of motion.\nAt a particular moment during the fall, the bag's velocity is $10\\,\\text{m/s}$ and its instantaneous acceleration is $\\frac{49}{9}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nWhat is the terminal velocity ${v}_{\\text{term}}$ of the bag? Assume the acceleration due to gravity is $g=9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ and the only forces acting on the body are the weight due to gravity and drag. \n\n${v}_{\\text{term}}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m/s}$",
